{"version":1,"name":"Ohio Grade 6 · 6.NS unit review","difficulty":"advanced","pace":"practice","questions":[{"text":"Compute 4/7 ÷ 2/6.","answers":["25/14","12/7","8/5","23/14"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.NS.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"quotient","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Number system","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=41","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.NS.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"quotient","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Divide fractions in context","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"There is 5/3 liter of juice. A serving is 5/4 liter. How many servings, including fractional servings, are available?","answers":["19/15","7/5","5/4","4/3"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.NS.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"servings","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Number system","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=41","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.NS.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"servings","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Divide fractions in context","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Without calculating exactly, what must be true about 3 ÷ 1/2?","answers":["It is negative because the divisor is a fraction","It is greater than 3 because half-unit pieces fit more times","It is less than 3 because division always makes smaller","It equals 3 because the numerator is 1"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Six half-unit pieces fit into three wholes. Division by a positive number below 1 increases the result.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.NS.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"division-estimate","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 6 · Number system","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=41","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"6.NS.1","grade":6,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"division-estimate","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Divide fractions in context","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Which situation is modeled by 3/4 ÷ 1/8?","answers":["How many 1/8-liter cups can be filled from 3/4 liter?","How much is left after removing 1/8 liter from 3/4 liter?","How much juice is in two bottles containing 3/4 and 1/8 liter?","How much juice is in 1/8 of a 3/4-liter bottle?"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Division asks how many groups of the divisor fit into the available amount.","topic":"Math","standard":"6.NS.1","mathGrade":6,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"choose-division-model","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middl